@openma/deepseek-harness-acp README · One package, standalone or plugin：Both shapes share `$DSH_HOME`: the same credential store, settings, presets,
and session logs as `dsh web` — conversations started in the Web UI can be
listed and loaded from the editor.

@openma/deepseek-harness-acp README · A · dsh profile plugin (recommended)：```bash
npm install -g @deepseek-ai/dsh
dsh web                                                    # save your API key once
dsh plugin --profile acp add @openma/deepseek-harness-acp@latest
```

```jsonc
// Zed settings.json
{
  "agent_servers": {
    "DeepSeek Harness": { "command": "dsh", "args": ["--profile", "acp"] }

@openma/deepseek-harness-acp README · B · Standalone server：```bash
npm install -g @openma/deepseek-harness-acp
dsh-acp login        # interactive; or save the key in the dsh Web UI
```

```jsonc
// Zed settings.json
{
  "agent_servers": {
    "DeepSeek Harness": { "command": "dsh-acp" }

@openma/deepseek-harness-acp README · Extend the Host composition：Adding a Cordis service does not automatically invent a wire method. Prefer a
standard ACP capability or event projection whenever one exists; add an
adapter only for behavior that must cross the client boundary.

@openma/deepseek-harness-acp README · Authentication：No keys in editor config, no secrets pasted into chat. ACP clients follow
the protocol: `initialize` advertises the **Agent Auth** methods the client
declared it can use.

@openma/deepseek-harness-acp README · Authentication：The credential gate is the **current provider route**. An Anthropic-only
store is enough for an Anthropic session; a DeepSeek key does not unlock
another provider.

